  "hypothesis": "Operator's Meowth ex Tuck Tail escape, with the precondition that the ablation exposed. Tuck Tail deals 60 and returns Meowth ex plus attached cards to hand, dodging its 2-prize liability and re-enabling Last-Ditch Catch on replay. The rule fires when nothing else on the bench can attack -- but that condition almost always means no Energy is in play, so Meowth ex cannot pay Tuck Tail's 3 Colorless either and simply dies for 2 prizes. Isolated without the guard it measured 73-127 (36.5%, p=0.0001). Adding 'and Meowth ex can actually attack right now' screened 115-85 (57.5%, p=0.034), a 21-point swing on the same rule.",
